abstract: >-
  Horizontal Product Branch (HPB) is a practitioner's methodology for
  planning and tracing product evolution across hardware, firmware and
  software. It applies branch-and-merge to the product, not to the code:
  every piece of work is a typed branch that forks from a released version
  and ends in a named release or in a discard with a written reason. HPB is
  defined by seven rules, a standard notation, an operating guide and
  metrics that fall out of the graph. This repository contains the paper
  and its LaTeX sources, the HPB Guide, and HPB Markup, an open-source text
  language and toolkit that draws HPB diagrams in HTML, React, Next.js,
  Vite, Markdown or the command line.
